cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  namma-metro-router: a cache-conscious bi-criteria transit routing engine and a
  multi-feed study of when multi-objective routing is load-bearing
message: >-
  If you use this software or its measurements, please cite it. The
  contribution is the experimental design and the findings; the implementation
  is a means to them.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Darshan
    family-names: Rajagoli
    affiliation: BITS Pilani, K. K. Birla Goa Campus
repository-code: 'https://github.com/darshanrajagoli/namma-metro-router'
abstract: >-
  A time-dependent, multi-label-correcting bi-criteria transit routing engine in
  C++17, with a compressed-sparse-row graph, arena-allocated labels and a
  separate transfer adjacency; a from-scratch RAPTOR implementation used both as
  a speed baseline and as an exactness oracle; and an empirical study across
  published GTFS feeds worldwide asking when a genuine time-versus-changes
  trade-off exists at all, and which structural property of a network predicts
  it. Includes a reproducible pipeline that fetches, pins and normalises every
  feed, and the measurement tooling used to falsify the project's own claims.
keywords:
  - transit routing
  - algorithm engineering
  - multi-objective optimisation
  - Pareto frontier
  - RAPTOR
  - GTFS
  - public transport
  - accessibility
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
